sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as API Client
    participant GW as Platform Gateway (batch-route)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant API as batch-gateway-apiserver<br/>8000/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant S3 as S3 / filesystem<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Proc as batch-gateway-processor<br/>StatefulSet
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>6379/TCP
    participant IGW as llm-d inference gateway / EPP<br/>batch-llm-route
    participant GC as batch-gateway-gc
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP

    Note over Client,PG: Flow 1: File upload and batch submission
    Client->>GW: POST /v1/files (JSONL), POST /v1/batches<br/>Bearer token (Kubernetes/OIDC)
    GW->>GW: AuthPolicy validates token, RateLimitPolicy
    GW->>API: Forward + X-MaaS-Username header<br/>HTTP or TLS 1.2+
    API->>S3: Store file under t-sha256(tenant)/<br/>SigV4
    API->>PG: Insert metadata + queue entry<br/>pth:Authorization tag (per sslmode)
    API-->>GW: File / Batch object
    GW-->>Client: JSON response

    Note over Proc,IGW: Flow 2: Batch processing (sync dispatch)
    Proc->>PG: Dequeue job, acquire ownership lease
    Proc->>S3: Download input file (SigV4)
    Proc->>Proc: Group by model + system-prompt hash, write plan to local disk
    loop Each request (global/per-endpoint semaphores, AIMD)
        Proc->>IGW: POST inference request<br/>Forwarded user bearer, optional TLS/mTLS
        IGW->>IGW: SubjectAccessReview on inferencepools
        IGW-->>Proc: Response (429/5xx triggers AIMD backoff)
        Proc->>PG: Progress / checkpoint
    end
    Proc->>S3: Upload output and error files (SigV4)
    Proc->>PG: Update job status

    Note over Proc,Redis: Flow 3: Async dispatch via llm-d-async
    Proc->>Redis: Push to request sorted set<br/>(or PostgreSQL SQL transport)
    Redis-->>Proc: Results from per-replica result queue

    Note over GC,K8s: Flow 4: Garbage collection and orphan recovery
    GC->>K8s: Watch processor StatefulSet, list pods<br/>ServiceAccount token, TLS 1.2+
    GC->>PG: Expire items, re-queue orphaned jobs
    GC->>S3: Delete expired file content (SigV4)
